{
    "question_text": "<h3>39. Combination Sum</h3><p>Given an array of <strong>distinct</strong> integers <code>candidates</code> and a target integer <code>target</code>, return <em>a list of all <strong>unique combinations</strong> of </em><code>candidates</code><em> where the chosen numbers sum to </em><code>target</code><em>.</em> You may return the combinations in <strong>any order</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>The <strong>same</strong> number may be chosen from <code>candidates</code> an <strong>unlimited number of times</strong>. Two combinations are unique if the <span data-keyword=\"frequency-array\">frequency</span> of at least one of the chosen numbers is different.</p>\n\n<p>The test cases are generated such that the number of unique combinations that sum up to <code>target</code> is less than <code>150</code> combinations for the given input.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> candidates = [2,3,6,7], target = 7\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[2,2,3],[7]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong>\n2 and 3 are candidates, and 2 + 2 + 3 = 7. Note that 2 can be used multiple times.\n7 is a candidate, and 7 = 7.\nThese are the only two combinations.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> candidates = [2,3,5], target = 8\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[2,2,2,2],[2,3,3],[3,5]]\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> candidates = [2], target = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= candidates.length &lt;= 30</code></li>\n\t<li><code>2 &lt;= candidates[i] &lt;= 40</code></li>\n\t<li>All elements of <code>candidates</code> are <strong>distinct</strong>.</li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= target &lt;= 40</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
    "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
    "marks": 10,
    "input_format": "Line 1: Array of distinct integers (candidates). Line 2: target integer.",
    "output_format": "List of all unique combinations.",
    "constraints": [
        "1 <= candidates.length <= 30",
        "2 <= candidates[i] <= 40",
        "All elements are distinct.",
        "1 <= target <= 40"
    ],
    "explanation": "Backtracking with recursion. Sort the candidates first to handle branches efficiently. At each step, either include the current candidate (unlimited times) or skip to the next. Base case: target becomes 0 (valid) or negative (invalid).",
    "answer": "class Solution:\\n    def combinationSum(self, candidates: List[int], target: int) -> List[List[int]]:\\n        res = []\\n        candidates.sort()\\n        def backtrack(remain, path, start):\\n            if remain == 0:\\n                res.append(list(path))\\n                return\\n            for i in range(start, len(candidates)):\\n                if candidates[i] > remain: break\\n                path.append(candidates[i])\\n                backtrack(remain - candidates[i], path, i)\\n                path.pop()\\n        backtrack(target, [], 0)\\n        return res",
    "boilerplate": {
        "python": "import sys\nimport json\n\ndef combinationSum(candidates, target):\n    res = []\n    candidates.sort()\n    def backtrack(remain, stack, start):\n        if remain == 0:\n            res.append(list(stack))\n            return\n        for i in range(start, len(candidates)):\n            if candidates[i] > remain: break\n            stack.append(candidates[i])\n            backtrack(remain - candidates[i], stack, i)\n            stack.pop()\n    backtrack(target, [], 0)\n    return res\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().strip().split('\\n')\n    if len(lines) < 2: sys.exit(0)\n    candidates = json.loads(lines[0].strip())\n    target = int(lines[1].strip())\n    print(json.dumps(combinationSum(candidates, target)))\n",
        "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid backtrack(vector<int>& candidates, int target, vector<vector<int>>& res, vector<int>& stack, int start) {\n    if (target == 0) {\n        res.push_back(stack);\n        return;\n    }\n    for (int i = start; i < candidates.size(); i++) {\n        if (candidates[i] > target) break;\n        stack.push_back(candidates[i]);\n        backtrack(candidates, target - candidates[i], res, stack, i);\n        stack.pop();\n    }\n}\n\nvector<vector<int>> combinationSum(vector<int>& candidates, int target) {\n    sort(candidates.begin(), candidates.end());\n    vector<vector<int>> res;\n    vector<int> stack;\n    backtrack(candidates, target, res, stack, 0);\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string line; if (!getline(cin, line)) return 0;\n    string target_line; getline(cin, target_line);\n    int target = stoi(target_line);\n    for (char &c : line) if (c == '[' || c == ']' || c == ',') c = ' ';\n    stringstream ss(line);\n    int val; vector<int> candidates;\n    while (ss >> val) candidates.push_back(val);\n    vector<vector<int>> res = combinationSum(candidates, target);\n    cout << \"[\";\n    for (int i = 0; i < res.size(); i++) {\n        cout << \"[\";\n        for (int j = 0; j < res[i].size(); j++) {\n            cout << res[i][j] << (j == res[i].size() - 1 ? \"\" : \", \");\n        }\n        cout << \"]\" << (i == res.size() - 1 ? \"\" : \", \");\n    }\n    cout << \"]\" << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static List<List<Integer>> combinationSum(int[] candidates, int target) {\n        Arrays.sort(candidates);\n        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();\n        backtrack(candidates, target, res, new ArrayList<>(), 0);\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    private static void backtrack(int[] candidates, int target, List<List<Integer>> res, List<Integer> stack, int start) {\n        if (target == 0) {\n            res.add(new ArrayList<>(stack));\n            return;\n        }\n        for (int i = start; i < candidates.length; i++) {\n            if (candidates[i] > target) break;\n            stack.add(candidates[i]);\n            backtrack(candidates, target - candidates[i], res, stack, i);\n            stack.remove(stack.size() - 1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = br.readLine(); if (line == null) return;\n        int target = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        line = line.replace(\"[\", \"\").replace(\"]\", \"\").replace(\",\", \" \").trim();\n        if (line.isEmpty()) { System.out.println(\"[]\"); return; }\n        String[] parts = line.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        int[] candidates = new int[parts.length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) candidates[i] = Integer.parseInt(parts[i]);\n        List<List<Integer>> res = combinationSum(candidates, target);\n        System.out.println(res);\n    }\n}\n",
        "javascript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction combinationSum(candidates, target) {\n    candidates.sort((a, b) => a - b);\n    let res = [];\n    function backtrack(remain, stack, start) {\n        if (remain === 0) {\n            res.push([...stack]);\n            return;\n        }\n        for (let i = start; i < candidates.length; i++) {\n            if (candidates[i] > remain) break;\n            stack.push(candidates[i]);\n            backtrack(remain - candidates[i], stack, i);\n            stack.pop();\n        }\n    }\n    backtrack(target, [], 0);\n    return res;\n}\n\nconst input = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8').trim().split('\\n');\nif (input.length < 2) process.exit(0);\nconst candidates = JSON.parse(input[0].trim());\nconst target = parseInt(input[1].trim());\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(combinationSum(candidates, target)));\n",
        "c": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() { return 0; }"
    },
